{"name":"Cross My Heart","hex":"#ad2a2d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cross my heart","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Phrase","definitions":["A declaration that the speaker is telling the truth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cross_my_heart"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sign of the cross","blocks":[{"text":"Making the sign of the cross, also known as blessing oneself or crossing oneself, is both a prayer and a ritual blessing made by members of some branches of Christianity. It is a very significant prayer because Christians are acknowledging their belief in the triune God, or the Holy Trinity: God the Father, God the Son and God the Holy Spirit. There are three variants of the sign of the cross, including a large sign of the cross made across the body, a small sign of the cross traced on the forehead or objects, as well as a lesser sign of the cross made over the forehead, lips and heart."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Sign_of_the_cross_step_by_step.png/330px-Sign_of_the_cross_step_by_step.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sign_of_the_cross"},{"title":"Cross My Heart (1937 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cross My Heart is a 1937 British drama film directed by Bernard Mainwaring and starring Kathleen Gibson, Kenne Duncan and Tully Comber. It was made at Pinewood Studios as a quota quickie for release by Paramount Pictures."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cross_My_Heart_(1937_film)"},{"title":"Cross My Heart (Marianas Trench song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Cross My Heart\" is a song by Canadian pop rock band Marianas Trench. It was released on November 24, 2008, as the lead single from their second studio album Masterpiece Theatre. An acoustic version of the song was released on March 10, 2009. The song peaked at number 15 on the Canadian Hot 100 and was certified triple-platinum by Music Canada."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0f/Cross_My_Hearts_Marianas_Trench.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cross_My_Heart_(Marianas_Trench_song)"},{"title":"Cross","blocks":[{"text":"The cross is a geometrical figure consisting of two intersecting lines or bars, usually perpendicular to each other. The lines usually run vertically and horizontally. A cross of oblique lines, in the shape of the Latin letter X, is also termed a saltire in heraldic terminology. Throughout centuries the cross in its various shapes and forms was a symbol of various beliefs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Cross2.svg/330px-Cross2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cross"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f7/V%C3%A4lsignelsen_och_korstecknet_vigsel_gif.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f7/V%C3%A4lsignelsen_och_korstecknet_vigsel_gif.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"An Evangelical-Lutheran priest makes the sign of the cross, along with the bride and groom being wed, during a Nuptial Mass in the Church of Sweden","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AV%C3%A4lsignelsen_och_korstecknet_vigsel_gif.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/SignOfTheCross.HandConfiguration.jpg/120px-SignOfTheCross.HandConfiguration.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/81/SignOfTheCross.HandConfiguration.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/SignOfTheCross.HandConfiguration.jpg/120px-Sig